From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:28:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GLM: attention-side prompt kernels behind switches (MiaAI-Lab
 recipe patches 0004, 0009, 0028)

Ports the attention node's prompt-chunk kernels of MiaAI-Lab's GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe at 1576746
(her tree d747563: the end state of patches 0004-glm-prompt-kernels, 0009-glm-prefill-kernels and 0028, with
0038's FP8 cache rows in the one-pass kernel), each behind its own switch, off unless set:

- TF_GLM_LATENT_MMA=1: a prompt chunk's absorb and expand on the tensor cores (_absorb_mma, _expand_mma).
- TF_GLM_HC_MMA=1: a prompt chunk's hyper-connection mixing dots on the tensor cores (_hc_partial_mma).
- TF_GLM_SEQ_ROWS=<rows> (her default 256): from that many rows, the BF16 / FP8 matmuls run every K slice in one
  program and sum them in _reduce's order (the same bits, no fp32 partials), with her prompt tiles.
- TF_GLM_SPARSE_ONEPASS=1: a prompt chunk's sparse rows in one online softmax a row (_sparse_onepass).
- TF_GLM_PROMPT_DSA=1 (this port's name for her unconditional path): a prompt chunk's selection through
  _select_prompt (pool_count's pools, TF_GLM_SCORE_RB rows a program), its dense pass only on the rows before
  SPARSE_FROM (forward.dense_rows) and its dense blocks' positions from one device add (Buffers.att_starts):
  the same tokens, counts and dense bits for every row a later kernel reads.

The kernels are hers verbatim (ruff 0.6.9's E741 on her one-pass kernel's `l` silenced by comments only). With every
switch unset the forward's calls are the base's. CPU: tests/test_glm_attn_prompt_kernels.py checks the switches
and, under the Triton interpreter, that the ported kernels give her tree's digests on the same seeded inputs
(tests/data/glm_attn_prompt_mia_digests.json) and this port's same-bits claims; on a GPU the same-bits checks.

Unset, every call is the base's, arguments included (the CPU harness's kernel fakes take the base's
signatures). The harness the call-recording tests share (test_glm_multi_prefill.py's build_forward and
patch_kernels, which test_glm_prefill_pairs.py and test_glm_kda_chunked.py use) follows the switches too: its
stand-in prompt buffers carry forward.Buffers' att_starts, it records sparse_onepass beside sparse_attention, and
its latent fakes take the `prompt` keyword. tests/test_glm_decode_kernels.py's routing test checks the stock
selection with TF_GLM_PROMPT_DSA unset, then that a prompt chunk takes _select_prompt with it set.

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("GLM attention-side prompt kernels") names MiaAI-Lab, the patches and the recipe
commit.

